<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA SELLS 5.42 BLN LEVS 4-WK DISCOUNT T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA SELLS 5.42 BLN LEVS 4-WK DISCOUNT T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry sold</p>
<p>5.422 billion levs of four-week discount T-bills, yielding</p>
<p>17.52 percent to maturity, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no par value or minimum</p>
<p>acceptable price set in advance for Wednesday's auction.</p>
<p>Auction date and maturity date overlap.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Price in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3024897004</p>
<p> Term			    four weeks</p>
<p> Issue date		    April 2</p>
<p> Maturity date		 April 30</p>
<p> Bids received		 44,574.2 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   84.20 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 5,421.9 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  85.09 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     17.52 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
